---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../data/seo';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — BettorIndex"
  description="BettorIndex privacy policy — how we collect, use, and protect your information on iOS and Android."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <SiteHeader slot="header" />

  <div class="legal-page">
    <div class="container container--narrow prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="page-subtitle">How BettorIndex collects, uses, and protects your information.</p>

      <section class="card">
        <p class="effective-date">Effective Date: July 24th, 2026</p>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy describes how BettorIndex ("we", "us", or "our") collects, uses, and protects your
          information when you use our mobile application on iOS and Android (the "App") and related website.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Account data:</strong> If you sign in with Apple or Google, we receive information needed to
            authenticate you (such as a provider identifier and, when shared by the provider, your email address). We
            store account and session data with our authentication provider to operate sign-in and account features.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Subscription and purchase data:</strong> If you subscribe or make in-app purchases, Apple App Store or
            Google Play processes payment. We may receive entitlement or transaction metadata (such as whether a subscription
            is active, expired, or renewed, product identifiers, and transaction identifiers). We do not receive your full
            payment card details. We may log subscription-related analytics events (such as when checkout starts, a free trial
            begins, or a paid subscription is completed) for product and marketing measurement.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Advertising and attribution data:</strong> We use mobile analytics and attribution tools to understand
            how users find and use the App, including whether an install or subscription may be related to an advertising
            campaign. Depending on your device settings and permissions, this may include device and app identifiers (such as
            an advertising identifier on iOS when you allow tracking, or an AppsFlyer identifier), install and session data,
            in-app event names, and related technical metadata. We do not use this data to sell your personal information.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Usage data:</strong> We may collect information about how you use the App, such as feature usage,
            session activity, app version, device type, and operating system (iOS or Android).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Support communications:</strong> If you contact us, we collect the information you provide (such as
            your email address and message content).
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To provide, operate, and improve App features and analytics.</li>
          <li>To authenticate you and manage your account.</li>
          <li>To verify subscription status and deliver paid features.</li>
          <li>To measure marketing performance and attribute installs and subscriptions to advertising campaigns.</li>
          <li>To respond to user inquiries and support requests.</li>
          <li>To maintain security, prevent fraud, and comply with legal obligations.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Data Sharing</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Third-party APIs:</strong> We use third-party services to provide sports data, odds, and related
            content. Limited technical data may be shared with these providers as needed to deliver App features.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>App stores:</strong> Apple and Google process payments and subscription management. Their use of your
            data is governed by their respective privacy policies when you subscribe or purchase through their stores.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Analytics and attribution partners:</strong> We use AppsFlyer as a mobile measurement partner to
            analyze installs, app usage, and in-app events (including subscription funnel events). AppsFlyer may share
            aggregated or event-level data with advertising partners (such as Meta) to measure ad performance when you
            have allowed tracking or when applicable privacy-preserving frameworks (such as Apple's SKAdNetwork) are used.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Authentication and infrastructure providers:</strong> We use service providers to host authentication,
            backend services, and related infrastructure. They may access information only to perform services on our behalf.
          </li>
          <li><strong>No sale of data:</strong> We do not sell your personal data to third parties.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Advertising, App Tracking, and Your Choices (iOS)</h2>
        <p>
          On iOS, the App may ask for permission to track activity across other companies' apps and websites for
          advertising measurement. Our request explains that BettorIndex uses this identifier to measure ad performance
          and improve the App, and that your data is not sold to third parties.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            If you <strong>allow</strong> tracking, we and our partners (including AppsFlyer and, through configured
            integrations, advertising platforms such as Meta) may use identifiers like the IDFA to help attribute installs
            and in-app events to ads.
          </li>
          <li>
            If you <strong>deny</strong> tracking or do not grant permission, the App still works. We may still collect
            limited analytics and subscription events through our measurement partners using other technical means permitted
            by Apple (such as SKAdNetwork and aggregated attribution), but ad attribution may be less precise.
          </li>
          <li>
            You can change iOS tracking preferences at any time in <strong>Settings → Privacy &amp; Security →
            Tracking</strong>, and manage subscriptions in your Apple ID or App Store settings.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Artificial Intelligence</h2>
        <p>
          BettorIndex does not currently use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or generative AI to process your
          personal data or to generate App content. We do not collect chat messages or similar inputs for AI processing.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Data Security</h2>
        <p>
          We use reasonable measures to protect your information. However, no method of transmission or storage is 100%
          secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
        </p>

        <h2>7. User Rights</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>You may request deletion of your account and associated data using in-app account deletion or by contacting us at <strong>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</strong>.</li>
          <li>
            Subscription management and certain purchase records are controlled by Apple or Google; you may also use your
            app store account settings to manage those records.
          </li>
          <li>
            On iOS, you may limit ad tracking through system settings as described above. Depending on your location, you
            may have additional privacy rights under applicable law.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          The App is not intended for children under 17. If you are under 17, please do not use the App.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted in the App and/or on our website
          with an updated effective date.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about this policy, contact us at: <strong>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</strong>
        </p>

        <p style="margin-top: 28px;">
          See also our <a href={`${base}terms/`}>Terms of Use and EULA</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>

  <SiteFooter slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding: 48px 0 80px;
  }
</style>
